    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1667">

                <pb facs="1061" n="945" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg945"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 817.51/635.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Jefferson to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 48.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Managua</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-02-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 8, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Relative to the Department’s desire to
                    secure a frank and full statement covering every phase of the Nicaraguan
                    financial situation as expressed in its telegram of August 17, 1913, and
                    reiterated January 17, 1914, I have the honor to transmit herewith the
                        information<anchor n="5" xml:id="d1667-f1"/> which I have at length been
                    able to obtain from the President.</p>
                <pb facs="1062" n="946" xml:id="pg946"/>
                <p>[Explanation of the enclosed financial statements.]</p>
                <p>In view of the chaotic management of the Government’s accounts and the deplorable
                    and almost incomprehensible state of its finances, it can hardly be hoped that
                    the figures here copied are very accurate.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Benjamin L. Jefferson</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
